</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.9 (build 863)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Asobi knows its connection.</b> On a phone hotspot, Low Data Mode, or a measured slow link, an amber <b>SLOW CONNECTION</b> tag appears beside the picture and anything heavy &#8212; an original, a package, a full-size clip &#8212; waits instead of downloading; the review copy plays meanwhile. <b>Review &#9656; Network&#8230;</b> holds the mode (Auto &#183; Slow connection &#183; Fast connection), <b>Measure Now</b>, and the list of what is waiting with sizes and estimates: Download Now, Forget, Download All. When the connection turns fast, Asobi asks once whether to fetch what waited.</li>
<li><b>The host sees who is on a slow connection.</b> Each person&#8217;s line in Share This Review &#8212; app seats and, where the browser says, web seats too &#8212; reads &#8220;slow connection &#183; ~6 Mbps&#8221; in amber, so you can pivot: send a package for later, or keep the review on review copies.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
