</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.9 (build 860)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Their media</b> &#8212; one choice on the invite sheet says how a client on Asobi Review gets the picture, and it acts when you save: <b>Stream review copies</b> (the same encrypted copies a browser gets, at once, nothing to send), <b>Send a package</b> (a bundle of the session is delivered to the review under their name; they find Download and Open when they arrive), or <b>Source links</b> (they download the originals from links you set). The choice is signed into the invite.</li>
<li><b>Review &#9656; Set Source Links&#8230;</b> &#8212; paste the folder a client can already reach and every clip gets its own link, editable by hand; sequences stream instead. The links save with the session and travel with every clip, so a seat without the file fetches it from there.</li>
<li>A guest is told, on joining, how clips they don&#8217;t have will arrive; and a clip that can&#8217;t be found says exactly what would fix it &#8212; a link from the host, the package waiting in Share This Review.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
